 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Function",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Clamps voltage transients from lightning and other surge events before they reach sensitive equipment. Named uses are I/O interfaces, VCC buses and other exposed circuits in telecom, computer, industrial and consumer equipment, and ESD (IEC 61000-4-2) and EFT (IEC 61000-4-4) protection of data lines."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Response and leakage",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Turn-on from 0 V to VBR min typically takes less than 1.0 ps. Typical IR is below 2 µA on parts with VBR min above 12 V. Clamping is strong and the incremental surge resistance is low. The chip junction is glass passivated and the package has built-in strain relief and a low profile."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pulse rating",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 3000 W rating holds for a 10/1000 µs pulse at a repetition rate (duty cycle) of 0.01 %. Allowed pulse power drops for longer pulses (Fig. 2) and with higher initial junction temperature, reaching 50 % at 150 °C (Fig. 3)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Clamping",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "During a voltage transient the part holds the voltage across it to a lower, flattened peak while the surge current flows through it (Fig. 1)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Failure mode",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Stressed past its voltage or current rating, the part typically fails short."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Assembly and materials",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Withstands reflow at 260 °C for 40 s; MSL 1 per J-STD-020 with a 260 °C lead-free peak. Matte tin, lead-free plated terminals (e3: Pb-free second-level interconnect with a tin finish per IPC/JEDEC J-STD-609A.01); halogen free and RoHS compliant; plastic package rated UL 94 V-0. Whisker testing follows JEDEC JESD201A tables 4a and 4c."
  }
 ],
